    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fad3lcm",
      "content": "The Supreme Court of India is the highest judicial authority in the country. It acts as the guardian of the Constitution and protector of Fundamental Rights. The provisions related to the Supreme Court are given in Part V, Chapter IV of the Constitution (Articles 124–147)."
    },
