    {
      "id": "el9xzky",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to the Supreme Court"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Supreme Court's constitutional framework defines the appointment, qualifications, tenure, and removal of judges.",
        "Article 131 outlines the Original Jurisdiction of the Supreme Court of India.",
        "Article 143 prescribes the Advisory Jurisdiction enabling the President to seek judicial opinion.",
        "The Supreme Court exercises multi-faceted judicial authority through Original, Appellate, Advisory, and Writ jurisdictions."
      ],
      "id": "ue69gof"
    },
