    {
      "id": "7x8qer1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Composition of the Supreme Court"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ozu4meb",
      "content": "• The Supreme Court consists of the Chief Justice of India and other judges."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4bm06gs",
      "content": "• Originally the Constitution provided for 1 Chief Justice and 7 judges."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "49026o8",
      "content": "• At present the sanctioned strength is 34 judges including the Chief Justice."
    },
    {
      "id": "ysj7nof",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Appointment of Judges"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "klfm2jv",
      "content": "• The judges of the Supreme Court are appointed by the President of India."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mo6llao",
      "content": "• The Chief Justice is appointed by the President."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xs95zin",
      "content": "• The collegium system plays an important role in the appointment process."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02iy9r",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Qualifications of Supreme Court Judges"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pqbrepx",
      "content": "• Must be a citizen of India."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5dj2wc4",
      "content": "• Must have been a judge of a High Court for at least 5 years."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8ivo3xu",
      "content": "• OR must have been an advocate of a High Court for at least 10 years."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d7miw34",
      "content": "• OR must be a distinguished jurist."
    },
    {
      "id": "etito6q",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Tenure of Judges"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2h91afj",
      "content": "• Supreme Court judges hold office until the age of 65 years."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p9t4932",
      "content": "• They can resign by writing to the President."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "usftbxt",
      "content": "• They can be removed through impeachment."
    },
    {
      "id": "3el4ody",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Removal of Judges"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dmlwgnx",
      "content": "• Judges can be removed only by impeachment."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Jurisdiction Type",
        "Constitutional Article"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Original Jurisdiction",
          "Article 131"
        ],
        [
          "Advisory Jurisdiction",
          "Article 143"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "bd4r1f3"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q3rn1b6",
      "content": "• Impeachment requires a special majority in both Houses of Parliament."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ychm5r0",
      "content": "• The grounds for removal are proved misbehavior or incapacity."
    },
    {
      "id": "zs6qxjb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Jurisdiction of the Supreme Court"
    },
    {
      "id": "uufz4p6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Original Jurisdiction (Article 131)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "df6xe3n",
      "content": "Disputes between the Union and States or between States."
    },
    {
      "id": "uw09xeg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Appellate Jurisdiction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yxn9187",
      "content": "Appeals from High Courts in constitutional, civil and criminal matters."
    },
    {
      "id": "z233sq9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Advisory Jurisdiction (Article 143)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2zwry9g",
      "content": "The President can seek the opinion of the Supreme Court."
    },
    {
      "id": "yzp2clm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Writ Jurisdiction"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Article 131 (Original Jurisdiction) and Article 143 (Advisory Jurisdiction) are frequently asked in Indian competitive exams.",
        "Questions often focus on the specific grounds and process for the Removal of Judges and Qualifications required for Supreme Court Judges."
      ],
      "id": "x7xpoyf"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "63kj3vb",
      "content": "The Supreme Court can issue writs under Article 32 for enforcement of Fundamental Rights."
    },
    {
      "id": "ozwavrc",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Writ</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Meaning</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Habeas Corpus</p>",
            "<p>Produce a person illegally detained</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mandamus</p>",
            "<p>Order to perform public duty</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Prohibition</p>",
            "<p>Prevent lower court from exceeding jurisdiction</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Certiorari</p>",
            "<p>Transfer case from lower court to higher court</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Quo Warranto</p>",
            "<p>Question authority of public office holder</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "k45hj46",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "EXAM Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dvcy77t",
      "content": "• Supreme Court established in 1950."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "let3syz",
      "content": "• Chief Justice of India is the head of the judiciary."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q8qqlvk",
      "content": "• Judges retire at age 65."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xodjiwu",
      "content": "• Article 32 is called the heart and soul of the Constitution."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
